      "text": "It lives in massive rivers that course through jungles. It swarms prey that enter its territory.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carvanha’s strongly developed jaws and its sharply pointed fangs pack the destructive power to rip out boat hulls. Many boats have been attacked and sunk by this Pokémon.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "If anything invades Carvanha’s territory, it will swarm and tear at the intruder with its pointed fangs. On its own, however, this Pokémon turns suddenly timid.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Each school has its own territory. Any intruders are mercilessly attacked with fangs bared.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "If they scent the faintest trace of blood, they rush to attack en masse. When alone, they’re rather cowardly.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "They’re such cowards that they won’t hunt alone. When five or so of them get together, they suddenly turn ferocious!",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "With its sturdy jaws and fangs, it can easily chomp wooden boats to splinters. It fights with Basculin over food.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It won’t attack while it’s alone—not even if it spots prey. Instead, it waits for other Carvanha to join it, and then the Pokémon attack as a group.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "These Pokémon have sharp fangs and powerful jaws. Sailors avoid Carvanha dens at all costs.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
